  "usage_note": "Use **on** before a day: *on Saturday*. *On Saturdays* means every Saturday. There is no preposition before **next**, **last**, **this**, or **every**: *this Saturday*. In American English, **on** is often left out in speech: *I work Saturdays*. The short written form is **Sat.**",
